1
00:00:00,773 --> 00:00:02,259
<i>Previously</i>
<i>on "The Mentalist"...</i>

2
00:00:02,459 --> 00:00:05,039
Van Pelt found some coded
files in Bertram's office.

3
00:00:05,239 --> 00:00:06,905
It looks like
a list.

4
00:00:06,907 --> 00:00:08,940
Patrick.
Kim.

5
00:00:08,942 --> 00:00:11,423
Thank you for this.
I needed the company.

6
00:00:11,448 --> 00:00:12,839
Who doesn't?

7
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,339
I'm here to make you
an offer.

8
00:00:14,341 --> 00:00:16,775
The Bureau is willing to drop
all the charges against you--

9
00:00:16,777 --> 00:00:19,611
if you come and work  for us.
For the F.B.I.?

10
00:00:19,802 --> 00:00:22,703
My terms.
I need you to read them

11
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:23,838
and sign it.

12
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,239
We can work with this.

13
00:00:25,241 --> 00:00:27,307
I'm gonna give you
my home phone number...

14
00:00:27,309 --> 00:00:30,177
In case you ever
make it back to the states.

15
00:00:30,179 --> 00:00:33,147
You are on U.S. soil now,
I am the federal government,

16
00:00:33,149 --> 00:00:35,249
and I am telling you
that <i>this...</i>

17
00:00:35,251 --> 00:00:37,050
is the deal.

18
00:00:37,052 --> 00:00:40,220
<i>That</i> is a napkin.
Take it or leave it.

19
00:00:40,222 --> 00:00:42,389
I'll leave it.

20
00:00:42,391 --> 00:00:44,224
Kim?
Agent Fischer.

21
00:00:44,226 --> 00:00:45,725
Agent Fischer.

22
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

23
00:01:09,249 --> 00:01:10,749
Have you seen
the stapler?

24
00:01:10,751 --> 00:01:12,185
It busted yesterday.

25
00:01:12,187 --> 00:01:13,786
We have another one?
Um...

26
00:01:13,788 --> 00:01:15,221
You know, maybe try
the copying machine.

27
00:01:15,223 --> 00:01:17,156
It has a staple function.
Isn't that a waste of paper?

28
00:01:17,158 --> 00:01:18,658
No, we have tons of paper.

29
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,294
I'm gonna go
with a paper clip.

30
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:24,297
Agent Fischer.

31
00:01:24,299 --> 00:01:26,398
Chief Lisbon.
Can we talk?

32
00:01:29,235 --> 00:01:30,602
It's adorable.

33
00:01:30,604 --> 00:01:32,771
Please. Sit down.

34
00:01:36,009 --> 00:01:37,475
How's Jane?

35
00:01:37,477 --> 00:01:38,977
He is still in detention.

36
00:01:38,979 --> 00:01:40,278
I know.

37
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,013
They won't deliver
my letters.

38
00:01:42,015 --> 00:01:43,281
Three months now.

39
00:01:43,283 --> 00:01:45,517
He's being kept
in isolation by design.

40
00:01:45,519 --> 00:01:47,051
By design?

41
00:01:47,053 --> 00:01:49,454
You mean until he does
what you want.

42
00:01:49,456 --> 00:01:51,823
We want to help him out.
You want to use him.

43
00:01:51,825 --> 00:01:53,225
Is that so bad?

44
00:01:53,227 --> 00:01:54,693
In case you haven't noticed,

45
00:01:54,695 --> 00:01:57,095
Jane is hardly federal agent
material.

46
00:01:57,097 --> 00:01:59,296
Was he state agent material?

47
00:01:59,298 --> 00:02:01,498
No, not really,
but he wanted to be there.

48
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:04,235
And while he was there,
he stopped the 10-year reign

49
00:02:04,237 --> 00:02:05,636
of a mass murderer

50
00:02:05,638 --> 00:02:08,072
and exposed a society
of corruption in law enforcement

51
00:02:08,074 --> 00:02:10,141
that spread halfway
across the country.

52
00:02:10,143 --> 00:02:13,510
Yeah, that didn't exactly
go down by the books, did it?

53
00:02:13,512 --> 00:02:16,179
Yeah, we know how Jane works.
And we know he's a risk.

54
00:02:16,181 --> 00:02:18,382
But we can't ignore
the upside.

55
00:02:18,384 --> 00:02:21,051
He closed every case
you were ever assigned.

56
00:02:21,053 --> 00:02:22,286
Yeah, he had help.

57
00:02:22,288 --> 00:02:24,020
Which is why I'm here.

58
00:02:24,022 --> 00:02:26,089
What do you want
from me?

59
00:02:26,091 --> 00:02:28,091
Help me, Lisbon.

60
00:02:28,093 --> 00:02:30,294
There are national security
issues at play.

61
00:02:30,296 --> 00:02:33,096
Jane won't work with us
unless we meet his demands.

62
00:02:33,098 --> 00:02:35,065
He has too much pride
to back down.

63
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:37,834
You got to give him a win.
Meet one of his demands.

64
00:02:37,836 --> 00:02:39,302
One of his demands is you.

65
00:02:39,304 --> 00:02:40,637
Meet another one.

66
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:42,538
We're running out of time.

67
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:45,075
Is your work here so pressing
that you can't take a break

68
00:02:45,077 --> 00:02:46,476
to help your country?

69
00:02:46,478 --> 00:02:49,646
Hey, Chief, uh,
I radioed Officer Phelps.

70
00:02:49,648 --> 00:02:51,547
He can run to Kmart
for a new stapler.

71
00:02:51,549 --> 00:02:53,816
Swingline
or Stanley Bostitch?

72
00:03:10,834 --> 00:03:13,769
Visitor. Splendid.

73
00:03:13,771 --> 00:03:16,738
Not a willing one,
based on the posture.

74
00:03:18,042 --> 00:03:19,574
That's a little better.

75
00:03:20,843 --> 00:03:22,678
It's good to see you.

76
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,078
How you holding up?

77
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,914
Ah...

78
00:03:25,916 --> 00:03:28,517
You know what
incarceration's like.

79
00:03:28,519 --> 00:03:30,185
Not really.

80
00:03:30,187 --> 00:03:31,820
Well, there's no need
to pretend, Lisbon.

81
00:03:31,822 --> 00:03:33,322
We're both in the same
predicament.

82
00:03:33,324 --> 00:03:36,224
How is that? I have a home
and a respected career.

83
00:03:36,226 --> 00:03:38,092
You're locked up
for murder.

84
00:03:38,094 --> 00:03:40,461
Eh, you're splitting hairs.
We're both trapped.

85
00:03:40,463 --> 00:03:42,297
How am I trapped?

86
00:03:42,299 --> 00:03:43,764
You live in Washington.

87
00:03:43,766 --> 00:03:45,066
I love Washington.

88
00:03:45,068 --> 00:03:46,067
High voice.

89
00:03:49,638 --> 00:03:51,572
Why are you
being so stubborn?

90
00:03:51,574 --> 00:03:53,874
The F.B.I. is offering you
a "Get out of jail free" card.

91
00:03:53,876 --> 00:03:55,832
Well, you make that sound
like a good thing.

92
00:03:55,857 --> 00:03:56,411
Isn't it?

93
00:03:56,412 --> 00:03:57,578
Not on their terms.

94
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:59,313
If I can't live
on my terms,

95
00:03:59,315 --> 00:04:01,449
I'm in prison anyway.

96
00:04:01,451 --> 00:04:04,284
Might as well just stay in this
cozy little detention suite.

97
00:04:04,286 --> 00:04:06,253
Well, that's your call,
but not today.

98
00:04:06,255 --> 00:04:07,822
The F.B.I. dragged me here,

99
00:04:07,824 --> 00:04:09,289
and they're not gonna
let me go home

100
00:04:09,291 --> 00:04:11,091
until you help them
with a case.

101
00:04:11,093 --> 00:04:13,827
So get your ass out of the chair
and let's go.

102
00:04:16,231 --> 00:04:17,931
Okay...

103
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,969
Federal officers
coming through.

104
00:04:24,906 --> 00:04:28,906
<font color=#00FF00>♪ The Mentalist 6x10 ♪</font>
<font color=#00FFFF>Green Thumb</font>
Original Air Date on December 8, 2013

105
00:04:28,931 --> 00:04:33,931
== sync, corrected by <font color=#00FF00>elderman</font> ==
<font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man</font>

106
00:04:55,221 --> 00:04:58,189
Hmm. I don't see
a couch anywhere.

107
00:04:58,191 --> 00:05:00,825
Don't start trouble.
At least not yet.

108
00:05:00,827 --> 00:05:02,160
Over here.

109
00:05:03,729 --> 00:05:06,664
We'll be assisting our
New York office on this case.

110
00:05:06,666 --> 00:05:10,601
And our asset has just
arrived.

111
00:05:10,603 --> 00:05:12,836
Mr. Jane. Lisbon.

112
00:05:12,838 --> 00:05:15,138
You called me an asset.
That's so touching.

113
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:17,074
I'm an optimist.

114
00:05:17,076 --> 00:05:19,310
We just started briefing,
if you'll have a seat.

115
00:05:19,312 --> 00:05:21,377
I'm fine. Hey, Cho.
Hey, Jane.

116
00:05:21,379 --> 00:05:22,813
What's going on?
Hey.

117
00:05:22,815 --> 00:05:24,314
We're in
the middle of a briefing.

118
00:05:24,316 --> 00:05:27,818
We can catch up later.
Gotcha. Hey there.

119
00:05:31,689 --> 00:05:34,657
This is Abel Schneiderman.

120
00:05:34,659 --> 00:05:37,160
He led the team
that wrote the new source code

121
00:05:37,162 --> 00:05:40,530
to protect the Federal Reserve
Banking System.

122
00:05:40,532 --> 00:05:44,367
Two days ago, he disappeared
from his loft in Brooklyn.

123
00:05:44,369 --> 00:05:46,236
There were signs of a struggle
in his bedroom.

124
00:05:46,238 --> 00:05:50,005
Schneiderman's cell phone
was busted on the floor.

125
00:05:50,007 --> 00:05:52,575
We are working on the theory
that he has been kidnapped.

126
00:05:52,577 --> 00:05:54,076
Has there been
a ransom demand?

127
00:05:54,078 --> 00:05:55,945
Not yet,
but we're expecting it.

128
00:05:55,947 --> 00:05:58,680
Well, it's either that, or they
will break him for the code

129
00:05:58,682 --> 00:06:00,015
and launch an attack

130
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:01,751
on the Federal Reserve
computer system.

131
00:06:01,753 --> 00:06:05,320
What Abel knows could bring
our banking system

132
00:06:05,322 --> 00:06:06,956
to its knees.

133
00:06:06,958 --> 00:06:08,090
Oh. This is exciting.

134
00:06:08,092 --> 00:06:09,358
Is this the case
that I'm here for?

135
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,626
We're getting to you.

136
00:06:10,628 --> 00:06:12,127
I knew you saw me. Huh?

137
00:06:12,129 --> 00:06:14,630
I knew it.

138
00:06:14,632 --> 00:06:16,131
Abel has a young wife--

139
00:06:16,133 --> 00:06:17,766
Defiance Schneiderman.

140
00:06:17,768 --> 00:06:19,968
Now understandably,
she's emotional

141
00:06:19,970 --> 00:06:23,071
and believes that the F.B.I.
is not utilizing

142
00:06:23,073 --> 00:06:25,440
all of its resources
to find her husband.

143
00:06:25,442 --> 00:06:27,876
And unfortunately, we can't let
anyone outside the F.B.I.

144
00:06:27,878 --> 00:06:30,511
know that Mr. Schneiderman's
been kidnapped.

145
00:06:30,513 --> 00:06:32,881
Otherwise, it could cripple
the financial systems.

146
00:06:32,883 --> 00:06:34,615
The New York office sent
a F.B.I. agent

147
00:06:34,617 --> 00:06:36,785
posing as a psychic,

148
00:06:36,787 --> 00:06:39,254
but Ms. Schneiderman
saw right through that.

149
00:06:39,256 --> 00:06:41,455
Well, of course.
She's a gypsy.

150
00:06:41,457 --> 00:06:44,224
Woman knows a thing or two
about psychics.

151
00:06:44,226 --> 00:06:45,426
What makes you say gypsy?

152
00:06:45,428 --> 00:06:47,094
Well, Defiance
is a gypsy name.

153
00:06:47,096 --> 00:06:48,362
Look at her bedroom.

154
00:06:48,364 --> 00:06:50,765
It's gypsy catnip.

155
00:06:50,767 --> 00:06:52,566
Abel there is Jewish,
which means

156
00:06:52,568 --> 00:06:54,735
she turned her back on her
entire clan to get married.

157
00:06:54,737 --> 00:06:57,004
Now she has a missing husband
and no family for support.

158
00:06:57,006 --> 00:06:59,239
It's a psychic 9-1-1.

159
00:06:59,241 --> 00:07:02,843
Well... there we are.

160
00:07:02,845 --> 00:07:04,211
Let's go to work.

161
00:07:15,323 --> 00:07:16,856
Thank you.

162
00:07:16,858 --> 00:07:19,125
Coach. I was expecting
a federal jet,

163
00:07:19,127 --> 00:07:21,328
or at least a helicopter.

164
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:22,529
Call the aisle seat.

165
00:07:22,531 --> 00:07:24,531
You'll sit
where you're told.

166
00:07:24,533 --> 00:07:26,566
You know, you can relax.

167
00:07:26,568 --> 00:07:27,600
Everything's good.

168
00:07:27,602 --> 00:07:29,902
You're still
a federal detainee,

169
00:07:29,904 --> 00:07:32,205
and you're in my charge,
so, no, I won't relax.

170
00:07:32,207 --> 00:07:35,107
And you'll do as I tell you,
you understand?

171
00:07:35,109 --> 00:07:36,775
Oh, I understand you, Kim.

172
00:07:36,777 --> 00:07:39,846
I understand you very well--
better than you do yourself.

173
00:07:39,848 --> 00:07:41,714
You will stay within
arm's length

174
00:07:41,716 --> 00:07:45,484
of F.B.I. personnel
at all times.

175
00:07:45,486 --> 00:07:47,753
Any foolishness, and you go
back to detention.

176
00:07:49,989 --> 00:07:51,523
She wasn't at all like this
on the island.

177
00:07:51,525 --> 00:07:53,959
How was she on the island?
I was undercover.

178
00:07:55,228 --> 00:07:56,495
You mean you were lying.

179
00:07:56,497 --> 00:07:58,129
I was using a false persona.

180
00:07:58,131 --> 00:07:59,465
Actually, I don't think so.

181
00:07:59,467 --> 00:08:02,300
I think that was
the real you.

182
00:08:02,302 --> 00:08:04,636
I think this federal
she-wolf shtick is,

183
00:08:04,638 --> 00:08:06,304
in fact, a false persona.

184
00:08:06,306 --> 00:08:08,073
No. This is the real me.

185
00:08:08,075 --> 00:08:09,807
Hmm.
We're boarding.

186
00:08:12,211 --> 00:08:13,511
Remember the rules.

187
00:08:24,591 --> 00:08:26,123
Ahh.

188
00:08:26,125 --> 00:08:29,427
I love the smell of reclaimed
meat and onion water.

189
00:08:31,563 --> 00:08:32,864
Do you have a $20?

190
00:08:34,666 --> 00:08:36,667
Thank <i>you.</i>

191
00:08:40,038 --> 00:08:42,106
Liaison with the New York
office is waiting upstairs.

192
00:08:42,108 --> 00:08:43,740
You two, stay here
and cover the exits.

193
00:08:43,742 --> 00:08:45,575
There are two--
west and south.

194
00:08:45,577 --> 00:08:48,279
Detain anyone
who tries to leave the building.

195
00:08:49,382 --> 00:08:51,148
Hey.

196
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:53,050
Arm's length, remember?

197
00:08:53,052 --> 00:08:54,351
Yeah. I'm just
a little hungry.

198
00:08:54,353 --> 00:08:56,453
I don't care.

199
00:08:56,455 --> 00:08:58,655
I've already paid.
<i>Now.</i>

200
00:09:05,431 --> 00:09:07,363
This is where
the Schneidermans live.

201
00:09:07,365 --> 00:09:09,198
It's mostly an abandoned
storage building,

202
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,801
but there are some
renters on the top floor.

203
00:09:10,803 --> 00:09:12,368
No security cameras.

204
00:09:12,370 --> 00:09:13,636
What kind of renters?

205
00:09:13,638 --> 00:09:16,639
Usual fringe types--
artists, dropouts.

206
00:09:16,641 --> 00:09:18,607
These aren't legal dwellings,
but they got a hell of a view.

207
00:09:18,609 --> 00:09:20,143
Hmm.

208
00:09:20,145 --> 00:09:21,644
In the photos you sent,

209
00:09:21,646 --> 00:09:23,212
there were signs of a struggle
in the bedroom?

210
00:09:23,214 --> 00:09:24,880
That's this way.
I'll show you.

211
00:09:35,091 --> 00:09:36,158
Hi.

212
00:09:38,127 --> 00:09:40,162
Mrs. Schneiderman?

213
00:09:41,698 --> 00:09:43,398
Defiance.

214
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,667
Defiance.

215
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:47,302
You are Romani gypsy?

216
00:09:47,304 --> 00:09:49,571
What do you know
about it?

217
00:09:49,573 --> 00:09:52,207
Carny circuit.
My dad was a showman.

218
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:57,012
So, Defiance. Yeah.

219
00:09:57,014 --> 00:09:58,580
Quite the painter.

220
00:10:01,485 --> 00:10:03,084
And who are you?

221
00:10:03,086 --> 00:10:04,786
Patrick Jane.

222
00:10:04,788 --> 00:10:07,355
I was invited by the F.B.I.
they said you need help.

223
00:10:07,357 --> 00:10:09,423
Oh...

224
00:10:12,294 --> 00:10:13,528
You're a psychic.

225
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:15,563
So I'm told.

226
00:10:17,133 --> 00:10:18,966
All right.

227
00:10:22,570 --> 00:10:25,439
Read my palm.

228
00:10:25,441 --> 00:10:27,641
It only works
with a dominant hand.

229
00:10:32,881 --> 00:10:34,615
No. Can't do it.

230
00:10:34,617 --> 00:10:36,717
I knew you were a fake.

231
00:10:36,719 --> 00:10:38,318
No, you're not
letting me in.

232
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:40,988
You're anxious about
finding your husband,

233
00:10:40,990 --> 00:10:43,724
and you don't want to be read
by a gorger from the government.

234
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,859
You're feeling scared and alone...

235
00:10:45,861 --> 00:10:47,761
And you don't trust strangers.

236
00:10:47,763 --> 00:10:49,784
And I don't blame you.
You can't trust these guys.

237
00:10:49,809 --> 00:10:50,532
Jane.

238
00:10:50,533 --> 00:10:52,232
I mean, they mean well,

239
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:55,301
and they'll find your husband
if you let them do their thing.

240
00:10:55,303 --> 00:10:58,071
Says you.
Yes, says me.

241
00:10:58,073 --> 00:11:01,841
Why are you asking the F.B.I.
to meet your spiritual needs?

242
00:11:01,843 --> 00:11:03,676
Don't you have a trusted
psychic of your own?

243
00:11:03,678 --> 00:11:05,845
I do. Cleo.

244
00:11:05,847 --> 00:11:07,880
But he's not answering
my phone calls.

245
00:11:07,882 --> 00:11:10,482
Hmm. That is odd.

246
00:11:10,484 --> 00:11:12,885
Can you find him?
Can you find Abel?

247
00:11:12,887 --> 00:11:14,720
Where was the last place
you saw him?

248
00:11:14,722 --> 00:11:16,989
On the roof,
night before last.

249
00:11:16,991 --> 00:11:18,490
What were you doing up there?

250
00:11:18,492 --> 00:11:21,961
Sharing a bottle of wine
with my girlfriends.

251
00:11:21,963 --> 00:11:24,563
Abel came up there
with his laptop.

252
00:11:24,565 --> 00:11:27,832
He likes to unwind on the roof.
It's peaceful.

253
00:11:27,834 --> 00:11:31,403
I'd like to take a look
at this roof.

254
00:11:35,542 --> 00:11:38,643
It's the stairs
at the end of the hallway.

255
00:11:40,846 --> 00:11:42,881
Hi.

256
00:11:42,883 --> 00:11:44,616
What are you doing?

257
00:11:44,618 --> 00:11:46,718
Spyhole went dark.

258
00:11:51,423 --> 00:11:52,624
What?

259
00:11:52,626 --> 00:11:54,593
We're with the F.B.I.

260
00:11:54,595 --> 00:11:56,394
Sir, did you see or hear
anything unusual

261
00:11:56,396 --> 00:11:57,962
in the last couple weeks?

262
00:11:57,964 --> 00:11:59,597
I already told you people,
no.

263
00:11:59,599 --> 00:12:00,965
We're with
a different office.

264
00:12:00,967 --> 00:12:04,468
So many,
like roaches.

265
00:12:06,072 --> 00:12:07,705
Nice guy.

266
00:12:07,707 --> 00:12:10,173
His name is Nguyen Hai.
He's a Vietnamese refugee.

267
00:12:10,175 --> 00:12:12,977
He used to run a noodle shop.
Now he owns the building.

268
00:12:12,979 --> 00:12:14,644
He was home the evening
of the disappearance,

269
00:12:14,646 --> 00:12:16,146
but he didn't hear or see
anything.

270
00:12:16,148 --> 00:12:17,680
How do you know that?

271
00:12:17,682 --> 00:12:19,382
I read the case files.

272
00:12:19,384 --> 00:12:21,118
I thought you weren't
interested in the case.

273
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,852
It was a long plane ride.

274
00:12:30,995 --> 00:12:33,896
So if Abel came up here
the night he disappeared,

275
00:12:33,898 --> 00:12:35,798
why was the bedroom trashed?

276
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:39,335
I don't know. I got home
late from the bar.

277
00:12:39,337 --> 00:12:42,672
When I got in, Abel was gone,
and our room was wrecked.

278
00:12:42,674 --> 00:12:45,008
Was he expecting
any visitors?

279
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:47,576
I don't think so.

280
00:12:47,578 --> 00:12:50,078
He would have told me
before I left.

281
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,014
This is
your husband's garden.

282
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:56,752
Yeah. How'd you know?

283
00:12:56,754 --> 00:12:59,288
His energy's here.

284
00:12:59,290 --> 00:13:01,457
He pours his energy
into this garden

285
00:13:01,459 --> 00:13:03,592
because he doesn't like being
a computer programmer.

286
00:13:03,594 --> 00:13:04,826
That's right.

287
00:13:04,828 --> 00:13:06,962
He feels trapped
in that world.

288
00:13:06,964 --> 00:13:08,396
Yes.

289
00:13:09,498 --> 00:13:10,999
It's an orderly world,

290
00:13:11,001 --> 00:13:13,434
full of rules and numbers.

291
00:13:13,436 --> 00:13:15,236
But it's not Abel's world.

292
00:13:15,238 --> 00:13:17,706
He sees himself more
as a rebel soul.

293
00:13:19,176 --> 00:13:20,941
He really loves that
Che Guevara guy.

294
00:13:20,943 --> 00:13:23,311
Yeah, that's why he rides
a motorcycle.

295
00:13:23,313 --> 00:13:25,880
Grows his own vegetables.

296
00:13:25,882 --> 00:13:27,815
That's why he married you.

297
00:13:27,817 --> 00:13:29,350
Oh, because I'm a gypsy?

298
00:13:29,352 --> 00:13:31,186
Yeah.

299
00:13:31,188 --> 00:13:33,221
Because you had the courage
to walk away from

300
00:13:33,223 --> 00:13:36,524
centuries of tradition
for love.

301
00:13:36,526 --> 00:13:38,292
You may not know it,
but you give your husband

302
00:13:38,294 --> 00:13:41,395
the courage to be who he is
on the inside.

303
00:13:41,397 --> 00:13:43,530
Is Abel alive?

304
00:13:47,736 --> 00:13:50,071
Why don't you help me
find him?

305
00:13:54,076 --> 00:13:55,576
I can feel him.

306
00:13:55,578 --> 00:13:57,578
Where is he?

307
00:13:57,580 --> 00:14:00,247
Just not getting
a clear read.

308
00:14:00,249 --> 00:14:02,148
What should I do?

309
00:14:03,318 --> 00:14:06,186
Well...

310
00:14:06,188 --> 00:14:08,955
Don't tell them
I said this,

311
00:14:08,957 --> 00:14:11,858
but you should sneak off
and notify the media right away.

312
00:14:11,860 --> 00:14:13,727
Hmm?
Okay.

313
00:14:13,729 --> 00:14:16,362
So that this city can pull
together and help find him.

314
00:14:16,364 --> 00:14:18,364
That is your only hope

315
00:14:18,366 --> 00:14:21,868
at saving
your husband's life.

316
00:14:21,870 --> 00:14:23,036
Okay.

317
00:14:23,038 --> 00:14:24,237
Go.

318
00:14:29,209 --> 00:14:30,943
Where's she going?

319
00:14:30,945 --> 00:14:33,879
She, uh... wants to call
the press.

320
00:14:33,881 --> 00:14:35,581
I-I-I tried to stop her.

321
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,550
Downstairs.

322
00:14:41,087 --> 00:14:43,655
You must really miss
that prison cell.

323
00:14:46,659 --> 00:14:48,160
I'll try
and talk to her.

324
00:14:48,162 --> 00:14:50,195
You have done
enough talking.

325
00:14:55,802 --> 00:14:58,370
Hi.

326
00:15:33,208 --> 00:15:34,775
After Jane returned
to the roof,

327
00:15:34,777 --> 00:15:36,843
he went down a fire escape
to the south alley.

328
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,213
And that's where the cameras
lose sight of him.

329
00:15:40,215 --> 00:15:42,115
Who was covering
the south exit?

330
00:15:42,117 --> 00:15:45,318
I was. But I didn't have
a line of sight to the alley.

331
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:47,753
There are no exits there,
so I didn't think--

332
00:15:47,755 --> 00:15:50,190
You misread the situation.
There'll be a note in your file.

333
00:15:52,526 --> 00:15:53,893
Yes, ma'am.

334
00:15:53,895 --> 00:15:57,063
Collins wasn't the only one
to misread the situation.

335
00:15:57,065 --> 00:15:58,731
You mean me?

336
00:15:58,733 --> 00:15:59,832
Yeah.

337
00:15:59,834 --> 00:16:02,568
You're correct.
I screwed up, too.

338
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:06,371
And supervising agent Abbott
will note that in <i>my</i> file.

339
00:16:06,373 --> 00:16:07,907
Fair enough.

340
00:16:07,909 --> 00:16:11,176
Why don't you and Agent Collins
focus on looking for Jane?

341
00:16:11,178 --> 00:16:12,877
You have an insight there.

342
00:16:12,879 --> 00:16:16,081
Coordinate with Davis
in the New York office.

343
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:17,282
Yes, ma'am.

344
00:16:17,284 --> 00:16:18,450
Thank you.

345
00:16:18,452 --> 00:16:21,386
This is the real you, huh?

346
00:16:21,388 --> 00:16:24,156
Let's keep our eyes
on the prize, shall we?

347
00:16:24,158 --> 00:16:25,457
Abel Schneiderman.

348
00:16:25,459 --> 00:16:27,192
We have narrowed
his kidnapping suspects...

349
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:29,995
Excuse me?
To three extremist groups--

350
00:16:31,430 --> 00:16:33,064
Why am I here?

351
00:16:33,066 --> 00:16:34,198
What do you mean?

352
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,267
I have no business.
Jane's gone.

353
00:16:36,269 --> 00:16:38,302
We'll find him.

354
00:16:38,304 --> 00:16:40,905
Uh, most of you will
recognize these faces.

355
00:16:40,907 --> 00:16:43,341
You're only gonna find him
if he wants to be found,

356
00:16:43,343 --> 00:16:45,783
which he doesn't, or he wouldn't
have left in the first place.

357
00:16:46,612 --> 00:16:48,379
Take five.

358
00:16:57,889 --> 00:17:00,824
Tell me something.
Uh...

359
00:17:00,826 --> 00:17:02,559
Did you help Jane escape?

360
00:17:03,061 --> 00:17:05,462
Why would I do that?

361
00:17:05,464 --> 00:17:07,764
You're h-his friend.

362
00:17:07,766 --> 00:17:10,900
Yes, I am, but I'm also
an officer of the law.

363
00:17:10,902 --> 00:17:13,436
I'm not trying to get you
in trouble. I just...

364
00:17:15,739 --> 00:17:17,874
I need your help.

365
00:17:17,876 --> 00:17:21,310
I...

366
00:17:21,312 --> 00:17:24,947
I was so certain
I had him figured out.

367
00:17:26,017 --> 00:17:29,152
Welcome to my life.

368
00:17:29,154 --> 00:17:32,655
How did you make it work
for so long?

369
00:17:32,657 --> 00:17:35,658
I've thought about that
myself.

370
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:38,260
I mean, after he disappeared.

371
00:17:38,262 --> 00:17:40,529
How I made it work
for so long.

372
00:17:40,531 --> 00:17:42,198
And what's the answer?

373
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:45,000
I have no idea.

374
00:17:45,002 --> 00:17:47,736
Were you two ever involved?

375
00:17:48,938 --> 00:17:52,074
That's a strange question.

376
00:17:52,076 --> 00:17:54,176
Why would you ask me that?

377
00:17:54,178 --> 00:17:56,544
Uh...

378
00:17:56,546 --> 00:17:58,213
No reason. I just--I...

379
00:18:00,349 --> 00:18:03,284
Uh, nev--never mind.

380
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:28,033
What are you doing?

381
00:19:28,035 --> 00:19:30,403
Waiting for you.

382
00:19:30,405 --> 00:19:32,204
To do what?

383
00:19:33,873 --> 00:19:35,307
Notice me.

384
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:40,779
Who are you?

385
00:19:40,781 --> 00:19:42,575
Jason Wylie.
Uh, junior I.T. analyst.

386
00:19:42,576 --> 00:19:44,258
I work in I.T.

387
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,786
Analyzing stuff.

388
00:19:47,788 --> 00:19:49,521
Okay.

389
00:19:49,523 --> 00:19:50,955
What do you want, Jason?

390
00:19:50,957 --> 00:19:52,957
Uh, we were told to focus
I.T. support

391
00:19:52,959 --> 00:19:54,526
on the Schneiderman case,

392
00:19:54,528 --> 00:19:56,628
but I'm my own man
at lunch, right?

393
00:19:56,630 --> 00:20:00,264
So I stole some satellite time
to hunt for Patrick Jane.

394
00:20:02,768 --> 00:20:04,168
Look what I found.

395
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,210
This was taken
22 minutes ago

396
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:13,811
from a satellite
over Brooklyn.

397
00:20:13,813 --> 00:20:15,980
You think it's really Jane?
It's not a trick?

398
00:20:15,982 --> 00:20:17,114
That's Jane.

399
00:20:17,116 --> 00:20:18,515
Notify New York right away.

400
00:20:20,918 --> 00:20:21,985
Who found this?

401
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:24,020
Analyst Wylie.
On his own time.

402
00:20:24,022 --> 00:20:25,823
Who is analyst Wylie?

403
00:20:25,825 --> 00:20:27,725
Right there.

404
00:20:32,664 --> 00:20:33,964
Feel free to join us.

405
00:20:40,938 --> 00:20:42,605
You took this initiative
on your own?

406
00:20:42,607 --> 00:20:43,874
Yes, sir.

407
00:20:43,876 --> 00:20:46,376
Well, let's see what you can do
on the primary team.

408
00:20:46,378 --> 00:20:48,979
Stanley, find Wylie a desk
in the bullpen.

409
00:21:06,663 --> 00:21:08,330
Down!

410
00:21:08,332 --> 00:21:09,399
Get down!

411
00:21:10,633 --> 00:21:12,734
Face down on the street!

412
00:21:29,218 --> 00:21:30,351
Thank you.

413
00:21:52,107 --> 00:21:54,042
Mnh.

414
00:21:54,044 --> 00:21:55,843
Congratulations.

415
00:21:55,845 --> 00:21:57,745
You got one over on me.
It's a nice stunt.

416
00:21:57,747 --> 00:21:59,347
You feel better now?

417
00:21:59,349 --> 00:22:02,416
Mm... no.
You woke me up.

418
00:22:02,418 --> 00:22:04,652
I don't get you.

419
00:22:04,654 --> 00:22:06,454
You hunted down and killed
your enemy.

420
00:22:06,456 --> 00:22:07,988
Why are you making
new ones?

421
00:22:07,990 --> 00:22:09,757
Eh, you're right.

422
00:22:09,759 --> 00:22:12,993
Running away
was a mistake.

423
00:22:12,995 --> 00:22:15,395
I'm ready to discuss
the job offer now.

424
00:22:15,397 --> 00:22:17,730
There is no offer,
not anymore.

425
00:22:17,732 --> 00:22:19,899
Nonsense. Let's talk.

426
00:22:19,901 --> 00:22:21,701
I am taking you back
to Texas.

427
00:22:21,703 --> 00:22:24,171
And next week you'll be
indicted for the murder

428
00:22:24,173 --> 00:22:26,206
of Thomas McAllister,

429
00:22:26,208 --> 00:22:27,674
among other charges.

430
00:22:27,676 --> 00:22:30,410
Guard.

431
00:22:31,412 --> 00:22:33,780
You cats find the body yet?

432
00:22:36,050 --> 00:22:37,550
What body?

433
00:22:37,552 --> 00:22:40,954
The body hidden on the roof
of Abel Schneiderman's building.

434
00:22:40,956 --> 00:22:43,255
You saw it?

435
00:22:43,257 --> 00:22:45,291
No, but there's a large
pile of soil

436
00:22:45,293 --> 00:22:46,793
just by the garden.

437
00:22:46,795 --> 00:22:49,095
Winter is almost upon us,

438
00:22:49,097 --> 00:22:51,063
so what is that soil
doing there?

439
00:22:51,065 --> 00:22:53,531
That's a rhetorical question.

440
00:22:53,533 --> 00:22:55,833
The soil is there
to make room for Cleo--

441
00:22:55,835 --> 00:22:57,268
Mrs. Schneiderman's psychic.

442
00:22:57,270 --> 00:22:59,971
He went missing
the same time as her husband.

443
00:22:59,973 --> 00:23:01,439
What are you talking about?

444
00:23:01,441 --> 00:23:04,209
Abel found out his wife
was sleeping with her psychic,

445
00:23:04,211 --> 00:23:05,776
so he killed him
in the bedroom.

446
00:23:05,778 --> 00:23:08,746
But Abel doesn't own a car,
so he cut up the body

447
00:23:08,748 --> 00:23:11,682
into pieces and buried them
in the garden.

448
00:23:11,684 --> 00:23:14,552
Your kidnap victim
isn't kidnapped.

449
00:23:14,554 --> 00:23:16,954
He's a killer.
And he's on the run.

450
00:23:19,090 --> 00:23:20,791
You're good.

451
00:23:20,793 --> 00:23:22,159
Thank you.

452
00:23:22,161 --> 00:23:24,662
A good liar.

453
00:23:24,664 --> 00:23:26,397
Eh...

454
00:23:36,374 --> 00:23:38,708
I really hope this isn't
his idea of a joke.

455
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:40,977
There is that chance.

456
00:23:42,879 --> 00:23:45,614
There's also the chance
that he's right.

457
00:23:47,084 --> 00:23:50,986
If there's one thing
that this job kills inside,

458
00:23:50,988 --> 00:23:52,888
it's a sense of trust.

459
00:23:55,260 --> 00:23:57,626
I almost forgot
what it feels like.

460
00:24:03,868 --> 00:24:05,901
Hey, let me get some light
over here.

461
00:24:15,844 --> 00:24:17,645
Well, there we go.

462
00:24:33,487 --> 00:24:35,338
Hey.

463
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:36,673
Hey.

464
00:24:36,675 --> 00:24:38,508
I can't believe
they gave me a desk.

465
00:24:41,045 --> 00:24:42,995
You can call me "The Coyote""

466
00:24:42,997 --> 00:24:45,131
I don't think so.

467
00:24:45,133 --> 00:24:46,999
That's just what they
call me downstairs.

468
00:24:47,001 --> 00:24:48,601
Don't ask me why, though.
They never told me.

469
00:24:51,389 --> 00:24:53,056
Your name's Wylie.

470
00:24:53,058 --> 00:24:54,974
Yeah.

471
00:24:57,778 --> 00:24:59,011
Wile e. Coyote.

472
00:24:59,013 --> 00:25:00,980
"Road Runner," the cartoon?

473
00:25:01,865 --> 00:25:04,200
No, it's Irish, I think.

474
00:25:06,186 --> 00:25:08,738
Uh, good morning,
Agent Stanley.

475
00:25:09,623 --> 00:25:11,040
Hey...

476
00:25:11,042 --> 00:25:13,126
Do you know the road runner
and the coyote?

477
00:25:13,128 --> 00:25:15,878
Yeah. Sex traffickers
in Dallas.

478
00:25:19,667 --> 00:25:22,168
There's a cartoon
about sex trafficking?

479
00:25:23,253 --> 00:25:25,221
Hey, Cho, you got a minute?

480
00:25:25,223 --> 00:25:26,839
Yeah.

481
00:25:32,896 --> 00:25:35,181
Abbott and I went
to Brooklyn last night.

482
00:25:35,183 --> 00:25:36,882
There was a body
hidden on the roof.

483
00:25:36,884 --> 00:25:37,900
Jane was right.

484
00:25:37,902 --> 00:25:39,385
He usually is.
You get an I.D.?

485
00:25:39,387 --> 00:25:41,654
We're waiting on forensics,
but it appears to be

486
00:25:41,656 --> 00:25:44,691
Mrs. Schneiderman's psychic,
just like Jane said.

487
00:25:44,693 --> 00:25:46,776
The director wants me
to bring him back on the case.

488
00:25:46,778 --> 00:25:48,194
That's a good call.

489
00:25:48,196 --> 00:25:49,562
He made fools of us.

490
00:25:49,564 --> 00:25:52,231
It won't be
the last time.

491
00:25:52,233 --> 00:25:54,250
How do I get him under control?

492
00:25:54,252 --> 00:25:56,753
You don't.
Jane is what he is.

493
00:25:56,755 --> 00:25:59,422
He'll use you to turn every
situation to his advantage.

494
00:25:59,424 --> 00:26:01,340
So what would you suggest
I do?

495
00:26:01,342 --> 00:26:03,209
Use him to your advantage.

496
00:26:09,016 --> 00:26:11,917
- Found the body?
-  Yes.

497
00:26:11,919 --> 00:26:13,970
Cleo Ascencio,
New York psychic,

498
00:26:13,972 --> 00:26:15,688
astrologer, healer.

499
00:26:15,690 --> 00:26:18,691
Also found a hacksaw
hidden in the planters,

500
00:26:18,693 --> 00:26:20,426
same brand as the other tools
in Abel's kit,

501
00:26:20,428 --> 00:26:22,261
with traces
of the victim's blood.

502
00:26:22,263 --> 00:26:24,614
So Abel killed his wife's lover
and ran away,

503
00:26:24,616 --> 00:26:27,233
just... like I said.

504
00:26:27,235 --> 00:26:29,602
Well, it appears so.

505
00:26:29,604 --> 00:26:31,621
Oh. Don't beat yourselves up.

506
00:26:31,623 --> 00:26:33,289
You would have figured it out
eventually.

507
00:26:34,324 --> 00:26:37,076
I said, "appears so."

508
00:26:37,078 --> 00:26:39,545
He just received a ransom note.

509
00:26:39,547 --> 00:26:41,247
A third-class letter
sent directly

510
00:26:41,249 --> 00:26:42,715
to Abel Schneiderman's office.

511
00:26:42,717 --> 00:26:45,251
What kind of kidnapper
uses snail mail?

512
00:26:45,253 --> 00:26:47,003
It's smart, really.

513
00:26:47,005 --> 00:26:50,456
Low-tech, old school,
no electronic footprint.

514
00:26:50,458 --> 00:26:53,559
Unidentified kidnappers
want $10 million

515
00:26:53,561 --> 00:26:55,628
deposited into an overseas
account by midnight,

516
00:26:55,630 --> 00:26:57,897
or they will sell Schneiderman
to the highest bidder.

517
00:26:57,899 --> 00:26:59,432
Next step would be
a cyber-attack

518
00:26:59,434 --> 00:27:00,733
on the Federal Reserve.

519
00:27:00,735 --> 00:27:02,685
You want me to notify Secret Service?
Please do.

520
00:27:04,304 --> 00:27:05,738
This isn't right.

521
00:27:05,740 --> 00:27:08,491
There are no kidnappers.

522
00:27:08,493 --> 00:27:10,142
What am I missing?

523
00:27:10,144 --> 00:27:11,527
Maybe Abel faked
his own kidnapping

524
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:13,112
to get money
to escape the country.

525
00:27:13,114 --> 00:27:15,481
That's very good, Lisbon.
That is the best theory yet,

526
00:27:15,483 --> 00:27:16,916
but it's wrong, too.

527
00:27:16,918 --> 00:27:19,085
I need another look
at that loft.

528
00:27:19,087 --> 00:27:21,654
Really?
Back to Brooklyn again?

529
00:27:21,656 --> 00:27:23,756
Yeah.

530
00:27:27,594 --> 00:27:28,628
Okay.

531
00:27:28,630 --> 00:27:30,496
Don't worry. I won't escape.

532
00:27:30,498 --> 00:27:32,849
Oh, I'm not worried.
If you walk away this time--

533
00:27:32,851 --> 00:27:35,718
I know. I'll end up spending
the rest of my life in prison.

534
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,103
No.

535
00:27:37,105 --> 00:27:38,805
I'll shoot you.

536
00:27:38,807 --> 00:27:40,223
Mm.

537
00:27:46,230 --> 00:27:48,531
Oh, look, they have
"Skymall."

538
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,868
"Skymall."

539
00:28:06,133 --> 00:28:07,967
Okay, Lisbon,
what's the matter?

540
00:28:07,969 --> 00:28:09,468
You.

541
00:28:09,470 --> 00:28:11,804
Was it that comment
I made in the bullpen?

542
00:28:11,806 --> 00:28:13,589
Because I think
it's a really good theory.

543
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:15,925
I don't care about that.

544
00:28:15,927 --> 00:28:18,311
You ran away again, Jane.

545
00:28:18,313 --> 00:28:20,212
Not from the F.B.I.
you ran away from me.

546
00:28:20,214 --> 00:28:21,714
Yeah, but I ran back.

547
00:28:21,716 --> 00:28:23,399
How was I supposed to know?

548
00:28:23,401 --> 00:28:25,518
I thought you were
gone again forever.

549
00:28:35,061 --> 00:28:37,163
Okay, you're right.
I-I'm sorry, Lisbon.

550
00:28:37,165 --> 00:28:38,948
I... I didn't think
about you.

551
00:28:38,950 --> 00:28:40,700
Well, you rarely do.

552
00:28:40,702 --> 00:28:43,669
Well, that's not true.

553
00:28:43,671 --> 00:28:46,238
I made you one of my demands.
I'm--I'm not joining the F.B.I.

554
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:47,874
unless they make you
a job offer.

555
00:28:47,876 --> 00:28:49,709
That's my point.

556
00:28:49,711 --> 00:28:52,762
What makes you think I want
to work with you again?

557
00:28:52,764 --> 00:28:54,914
You are difficult
and exhausting,

558
00:28:54,916 --> 00:28:56,632
and maybe I don't want
to put the rest of my life

559
00:28:56,634 --> 00:28:58,918
on hold to be your sidekick.

560
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:00,970
Have you ever even
thought about that?

561
00:29:00,972 --> 00:29:02,355
No... no.

562
00:29:02,357 --> 00:29:03,890
I hadn't considered it.

563
00:29:03,892 --> 00:29:06,475
You think you know
what's good for my life,

564
00:29:06,477 --> 00:29:09,645
but you haven't been
a part of my life for two years.

565
00:29:13,367 --> 00:29:16,903
So let's get this case
wrapped up so I can go home.

566
00:29:19,156 --> 00:29:21,774
How dare you think
that I would cheat on Abel!

567
00:29:21,776 --> 00:29:23,459
And with Cleo?!

568
00:29:23,461 --> 00:29:26,612
No, I-I wasn't reading you.
I was reading your husband.

569
00:29:26,614 --> 00:29:28,915
You're a catch.
Your husband's a computer nerd

570
00:29:28,917 --> 00:29:31,751
pretending to be a rebel
to try and hang on to you.

571
00:29:31,753 --> 00:29:34,136
Men like that snap
when they feel betrayed.

572
00:29:34,138 --> 00:29:37,456
It's true.
Abel is very jealous

573
00:29:37,458 --> 00:29:40,292
and insecure
and he overcompensates,

574
00:29:40,294 --> 00:29:43,179
but you missed one detail.

575
00:29:43,181 --> 00:29:45,398
You're in love.

576
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,233
He's my little lion,

577
00:29:47,235 --> 00:29:49,969
and I would never sleep
with another man.

578
00:29:49,971 --> 00:29:52,521
I see that now.

579
00:29:55,275 --> 00:29:57,443
I would like to be alone.
All right.

580
00:29:57,445 --> 00:29:58,861
Please leave.

581
00:29:58,863 --> 00:30:00,780
Okay.

582
00:30:02,333 --> 00:30:04,250
Do you still think
Abel killed Cleo?

583
00:30:04,252 --> 00:30:06,335
Oh, I know he did.
Guy's a hothead.

584
00:30:06,337 --> 00:30:09,005
Those swollen biceps
and neck tattoos.

585
00:30:09,007 --> 00:30:11,874
The mere hint of an affair
would set that guy off.

586
00:30:11,876 --> 00:30:14,377
Why was her psychic here
the night Abel disappeared?

587
00:30:14,379 --> 00:30:16,095
Defiance was out
with her friends all night.

588
00:30:16,097 --> 00:30:17,930
There was no reason for him
to be at the loft.

589
00:30:17,932 --> 00:30:21,267
Cleo Ascencio.
It's such a theatrical name.

590
00:30:21,269 --> 00:30:22,768
You think it's real?

591
00:30:22,770 --> 00:30:24,053
It is.
We ran his fingerprints.

592
00:30:24,055 --> 00:30:26,605
Let me guess. Clean record?
Spotless.

593
00:30:26,607 --> 00:30:28,174
What are you suggesting,
Lisbon?

594
00:30:28,176 --> 00:30:30,226
Ascencio--
it sounds Cuban.

595
00:30:30,228 --> 00:30:32,778
There's a scam
that they do in Cuba.

596
00:30:32,780 --> 00:30:34,563
Brokers charge
large sums of money

597
00:30:34,565 --> 00:30:36,065
to surgically
modify fingerprints.

598
00:30:36,067 --> 00:30:38,317
They swap the right fingertips
and the left.

599
00:30:38,319 --> 00:30:41,153
It fools immigration
every time.

600
00:30:41,155 --> 00:30:42,571
How do you know that?

601
00:30:42,573 --> 00:30:44,573
I'm a police chief.

602
00:30:47,627 --> 00:30:50,329
With a lot of reading time
on my hands.

603
00:30:51,581 --> 00:30:53,499
I did what Chief Lisbon
suggested

604
00:30:53,501 --> 00:30:55,868
and ran the left-hand
fingerprints for the right,

605
00:30:55,870 --> 00:30:57,753
and it worked.

606
00:30:57,755 --> 00:31:00,606
Cleo Ascencio transforms
into...

607
00:31:00,608 --> 00:31:03,342
Jose Martinez.

608
00:31:03,344 --> 00:31:04,427
And who is he?

609
00:31:04,429 --> 00:31:06,679
A fraud. A street hustler
from Havana.

610
00:31:06,681 --> 00:31:09,265
Made a living picking pockets
until he stole a wallet

611
00:31:09,267 --> 00:31:11,233
from one of Castro's
ministers.

612
00:31:11,235 --> 00:31:13,686
Now he's wanted
by the P.N.R.

613
00:31:19,192 --> 00:31:21,110
Jose Martinez?

614
00:31:21,112 --> 00:31:23,162
He fled Cuba
and set up shop here.

615
00:31:23,164 --> 00:31:24,914
Okay, so he changed
his name.

616
00:31:24,916 --> 00:31:26,749
That doesn't mean
he's a fraud.

617
00:31:26,751 --> 00:31:28,334
You have any idea
why he was in your loft

618
00:31:28,336 --> 00:31:29,802
the night your husband
went missing?

619
00:31:29,804 --> 00:31:32,254
Sure. Uh, Cleo would
drop by sometimes

620
00:31:32,256 --> 00:31:34,373
when he thought he had
an insight I should here.

621
00:31:34,375 --> 00:31:36,258
Now, if you weren't here,

622
00:31:36,260 --> 00:31:37,760
would Abel let him
into the building?

623
00:31:37,762 --> 00:31:39,795
He wouldn't have to.
Cleo had the security code.

624
00:31:39,797 --> 00:31:41,263
He would just
buzz himself in.

625
00:31:41,265 --> 00:31:42,848
Well, that explains
what he was doing

626
00:31:42,850 --> 00:31:46,052
in your bedroom two nights ago.
It does?

627
00:31:46,054 --> 00:31:47,353
Hot reading.

628
00:31:47,355 --> 00:31:49,638
It's the bread and butter
of the spiritual flimflam man.

629
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:53,008
You gather personal effects
on your subject in advance,

630
00:31:53,010 --> 00:31:56,312
and then you present them
as psychic revelations.

631
00:31:56,314 --> 00:31:59,398
Martinez came up to see
if Defiance wanted a reading.

632
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:01,266
But she was out drinking,
and Abel was on the roof.

633
00:32:01,268 --> 00:32:04,403
So he came up into the house
and he took a little snoop.

634
00:32:04,405 --> 00:32:05,621
When Abel came downstairs,

635
00:32:05,623 --> 00:32:07,123
he caught your psychic
in the bedroom

636
00:32:07,125 --> 00:32:08,741
and assumed you were
sleeping with him.

637
00:32:10,127 --> 00:32:13,212
Okay. Fine.

638
00:32:13,214 --> 00:32:14,580
But none of that explains

639
00:32:14,582 --> 00:32:16,415
who took Abel
from the building.

640
00:32:16,417 --> 00:32:18,283
No, it doesn't,
because I don't think

641
00:32:18,285 --> 00:32:19,752
Abel ever left the building.

642
00:32:19,754 --> 00:32:21,954
If my suspicion is correct,

643
00:32:21,956 --> 00:32:25,257
he is still here,
and he is still very much alive.

644
00:32:36,826 --> 00:32:39,628
One of us needs to stay here
with Defiance.

645
00:32:39,630 --> 00:32:41,463
I'll stay.
You don't want in on the bust?

646
00:32:41,465 --> 00:32:44,299
Nah, the three of us have done
a lot of busts together. You go.

647
00:32:44,301 --> 00:32:47,502
There's nothing like
a takedown with Jane.

648
00:32:47,504 --> 00:32:49,471
Shucks.

649
00:32:49,473 --> 00:32:50,922
Shall we?

650
00:33:00,433 --> 00:33:02,767
One...

651
00:33:02,769 --> 00:33:03,935
Two...

652
00:33:03,937 --> 00:33:05,854
Three.

653
00:33:05,856 --> 00:33:07,989
Do you know what time it is?

654
00:33:07,991 --> 00:33:10,025
See? Distractible
and paranoid by nature.

655
00:33:10,027 --> 00:33:13,078
Can't let anyone pass this door
without knowing who it is.

656
00:33:14,247 --> 00:33:15,997
What the hell is going on
out here?

657
00:33:15,999 --> 00:33:18,083
Glad you asked.
There's been a murder.

658
00:33:18,918 --> 00:33:20,652
And you said already.
Schneiderman.

659
00:33:20,654 --> 00:33:23,505
No, he was kidnapped.
Another man's been murdered,

660
00:33:23,507 --> 00:33:25,040
but you know that, right?

661
00:33:25,042 --> 00:33:27,092
I don't know what you're
talking about.

662
00:33:27,094 --> 00:33:28,460
Sure, you do.
You know everything,

663
00:33:28,462 --> 00:33:30,262
including where Schneiderman
is right now.

664
00:33:30,264 --> 00:33:32,430
I don't know anything.

665
00:33:32,432 --> 00:33:34,432
He's in your apartment,
isn't he?

666
00:33:35,801 --> 00:33:39,371
Probably in the bathroom.
No. You value your privacy.

667
00:33:39,373 --> 00:33:43,475
I'm gonna say...
stashed in a closet.

668
00:33:43,477 --> 00:33:45,176
Watch out, Jane.

669
00:33:45,178 --> 00:33:47,395
Open the door, Nguyen!

670
00:33:47,397 --> 00:33:49,781
Uh, somebody gonna break
the door?

671
00:33:49,783 --> 00:33:51,516
Go ahead.

672
00:33:51,518 --> 00:33:53,702
All right, I'm ready.

673
00:33:54,870 --> 00:33:56,288
Break right.

674
00:34:19,729 --> 00:34:21,513
I got him.
Go find Schneiderman.

675
00:34:38,897 --> 00:34:40,565
Did you invite
Jose Martinez

676
00:34:40,567 --> 00:34:42,167
into your loft
the night of his death?

677
00:34:42,169 --> 00:34:44,169
No. I came down
from the roof,

678
00:34:44,171 --> 00:34:45,837
and he was there
in our bedroom.

679
00:34:45,839 --> 00:34:47,038
And what was he doing?

680
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:49,507
That's what I wanted
to know.

681
00:34:52,795 --> 00:34:54,579
Hey!

682
00:34:54,581 --> 00:34:58,266
Hey! Abel!

683
00:34:58,268 --> 00:35:00,301
Uh, this isn't
what it looks like.

684
00:35:00,303 --> 00:35:03,021
What are you doing?
Uh... nothing. See?

685
00:35:03,023 --> 00:35:04,806
Where's Defiance?
Defiance?!

686
00:35:04,808 --> 00:35:07,993
She's not here.
I let myself in! I should go.

687
00:35:07,995 --> 00:35:10,111
You're not going anywhere!

688
00:35:10,113 --> 00:35:12,280
I'm sorry, okay?
I should go.

689
00:35:13,717 --> 00:35:15,784
<i>I kind of lost it.</i>

690
00:35:18,622 --> 00:35:20,505
All right! All right!

691
00:35:20,507 --> 00:35:22,290
I'll go!

692
00:35:22,292 --> 00:35:24,108
<i>His foot got caught</i>
<i>in the shag throw.</i>

693
00:35:24,110 --> 00:35:27,245
<i>His--his head hit</i>
<i>the coffee table.</i>

694
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:29,731
<i>It was horrible.</i>

695
00:35:30,633 --> 00:35:32,217
And why didn't you
call the police?

696
00:35:32,219 --> 00:35:33,885
With a dead man
on the floor?

697
00:35:33,887 --> 00:35:36,004
What you described
is involuntary manslaughter.

698
00:35:36,006 --> 00:35:37,756
You would have been out
in six months.

699
00:35:37,758 --> 00:35:39,290
Then what?

700
00:35:39,292 --> 00:35:41,676
I work the Feds.
My career would have been over.

701
00:35:41,678 --> 00:35:45,313
I would have lost Defiance.

702
00:35:45,315 --> 00:35:48,600
That's when I decided
to hide the body.

703
00:35:52,906 --> 00:35:54,773
<i>And the squeaky</i>
<i>hallway door made sure</i>

704
00:35:54,775 --> 00:35:57,659
<i>you always heard</i>
<i>the Schneidermans.</i>

705
00:35:58,661 --> 00:36:00,161
<i>That is how you came to see</i>

706
00:36:00,163 --> 00:36:02,697
<i>Abel hauling a body</i>
<i>to the roof.</i>

707
00:36:06,253 --> 00:36:09,003
Who is he?

708
00:36:12,342 --> 00:36:15,176
Just somebody who deserved
what he got.

709
00:36:15,178 --> 00:36:17,212
This...
This is a bad dream.

710
00:36:17,214 --> 00:36:19,631
Just go back to bed,
Mr. Nguyen.

711
00:36:19,633 --> 00:36:22,016
I'm not sleepy.

712
00:36:23,436 --> 00:36:24,803
What do you want?

713
00:36:24,805 --> 00:36:26,888
You want money? Fine.

714
00:36:26,890 --> 00:36:28,306
I'll give you $5,000

715
00:36:28,308 --> 00:36:30,859
to forget everything
you saw here tonight.

716
00:36:31,777 --> 00:36:33,511
You're that security contractor

717
00:36:33,513 --> 00:36:35,447
for the federal government.

718
00:36:36,315 --> 00:36:38,066
Yeah.

719
00:36:41,954 --> 00:36:44,789
Exactly how much are you
worth to the government?

720
00:36:49,962 --> 00:36:52,080
Our colleague Mr. Jane
suspected

721
00:36:52,082 --> 00:36:53,581
there was more to you
than meets the eye.

722
00:36:53,583 --> 00:36:55,383
You didn't get those
scars on your face

723
00:36:55,385 --> 00:36:56,801
from running a noodle shop.

724
00:36:56,803 --> 00:36:59,537
You're a gangster from way back.
Green Dragons?

725
00:37:04,343 --> 00:37:05,727
"Born to kill."

726
00:37:07,146 --> 00:37:10,398
It was the bloodiest street gang
in New York history.

727
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:13,434
All Vietnamese refugees.

728
00:37:14,436 --> 00:37:16,271
I hear you guys owned
Chinatown in the '80s.

729
00:37:16,273 --> 00:37:17,989
We owned New York.

730
00:37:17,991 --> 00:37:21,109
One last story
for the record books.

731
00:37:21,111 --> 00:37:23,394
How an original member
of B.T.K.

732
00:37:23,396 --> 00:37:27,031
almost took the feds
for $10 million.

733
00:37:27,033 --> 00:37:29,250
Give me that confession.

734
00:37:31,171 --> 00:37:32,921
Give me the pen.

735
00:37:50,306 --> 00:37:52,256
You wanted to talk to me?

736
00:37:52,258 --> 00:37:55,059
You have a sharp mind.

737
00:37:55,061 --> 00:37:56,895
And people like you.

738
00:37:56,897 --> 00:37:58,196
Some people.

739
00:37:58,198 --> 00:38:00,198
Well...

740
00:38:01,567 --> 00:38:02,951
I didn't think so before,

741
00:38:02,953 --> 00:38:07,622
but I can see this arrangement
working on a permanent basis.

742
00:38:07,624 --> 00:38:09,791
I like you, too, Dennis.

743
00:38:09,793 --> 00:38:11,943
And I can see working
with you in the future,

744
00:38:11,945 --> 00:38:13,828
but only on my terms,
and you know that.

745
00:38:13,830 --> 00:38:16,831
Yeah, we've been through this.
There's no deals.

746
00:38:16,833 --> 00:38:19,000
No demands, no negotiations.

747
00:38:19,002 --> 00:38:22,503
We are offering you a career,
a clean slate,

748
00:38:22,505 --> 00:38:26,057
a chance
to make a difference.

749
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:34,816
You drive a hard bargain,
Dennis.

750
00:38:36,235 --> 00:38:38,186
Okay, pet leopard's
off the table.

751
00:38:38,188 --> 00:38:39,804
Forget about that.

752
00:38:39,806 --> 00:38:42,273
But I need the full pardon.
And the Airstream.

753
00:38:42,275 --> 00:38:43,808
And I need a couch, man,

754
00:38:43,810 --> 00:38:46,661
'cause everything is cold
and hard around here.

755
00:38:46,663 --> 00:38:48,413
And...

756
00:38:48,415 --> 00:38:51,115
I need a job offer
for Lisbon.

757
00:38:51,117 --> 00:38:53,501
I am sure that some people

758
00:38:53,503 --> 00:38:56,204
find this side of you
endearing...

759
00:38:59,091 --> 00:39:01,376
But I'm not one of them.

760
00:39:03,162 --> 00:39:06,881
I'll be following
your murder trial on the TV.

761
00:39:06,883 --> 00:39:08,165
Good luck.

762
00:39:08,167 --> 00:39:09,550
Okay.

763
00:39:09,552 --> 00:39:10,718
Thank you.

764
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:13,187
Oh, enjoy your mail.

765
00:39:37,796 --> 00:39:40,164
Fellas. Stop right there.

766
00:39:43,802 --> 00:39:45,403
Jane...

767
00:39:45,405 --> 00:39:47,422
Where did you get this from?

768
00:39:47,424 --> 00:39:50,141
Oh, a thumb drive
Gail Bertram was hiding.

769
00:39:50,143 --> 00:39:52,644
This is the first
I'm hearing about it.

770
00:39:52,646 --> 00:39:54,762
It's the first
I've talked of it.

771
00:39:54,764 --> 00:39:58,766
These are all the members
of the Blake Association.

772
00:39:58,768 --> 00:40:00,401
Correct.

773
00:40:00,403 --> 00:40:02,987
I figured Bertram was
keeping it as insurance.

774
00:40:02,989 --> 00:40:06,074
Well, we've arrested
or retired all of these people.

775
00:40:06,076 --> 00:40:07,492
Yes, you have--

776
00:40:07,494 --> 00:40:10,061
except the ones
that I've blacked out.

777
00:40:10,063 --> 00:40:12,330
Those ones you haven't caught.

778
00:40:12,332 --> 00:40:14,332
We caught them all.

779
00:40:14,334 --> 00:40:17,418
Did you? Well, I guess
Bertram was wrong then.

780
00:40:19,672 --> 00:40:21,205
Give me the names.

781
00:40:21,207 --> 00:40:23,041
A couple of judges,
a congressman,

782
00:40:23,043 --> 00:40:24,959
several F.B.I. agents.
Names.

783
00:40:24,961 --> 00:40:26,410
Big names, some of them.

784
00:40:26,412 --> 00:40:28,429
If that list ever got out
to the press,

785
00:40:28,431 --> 00:40:31,299
it'd cause all kinds
of turmoil, wouldn't it?

786
00:40:31,301 --> 00:40:33,601
Are you threatening me?
Oh, no.

787
00:40:33,603 --> 00:40:35,920
Just pointing out
that we both have the power

788
00:40:35,922 --> 00:40:37,722
to create misery.

789
00:40:39,091 --> 00:40:40,558
Okay.

790
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:42,560
You give me the names,
and we'll agree

791
00:40:42,562 --> 00:40:45,947
to all of your terms
on the contract.

792
00:40:45,949 --> 00:40:49,117
If I give you the names,
you'll break the contract.

793
00:40:49,119 --> 00:40:51,102
You've already done it once.

794
00:40:51,104 --> 00:40:52,620
What do you propose?

795
00:40:52,622 --> 00:40:55,039
I propose that you surrender
to my terms,

796
00:40:55,041 --> 00:40:56,941
and when I'm finished
with your contract,

797
00:40:56,943 --> 00:40:58,826
and only then,

798
00:40:58,828 --> 00:41:01,045
I will give you the names.

799
00:41:04,166 --> 00:41:05,717
Get him out of here.

800
00:41:22,267 --> 00:41:24,352
Mm...

801
00:41:24,354 --> 00:41:26,487
Well...
Hmm?

802
00:41:26,489 --> 00:41:28,022
You did it this time.

803
00:41:28,024 --> 00:41:30,074
You brought the F.B.I.
to its knees.

804
00:41:32,028 --> 00:41:33,077
Did I?

805
00:41:33,079 --> 00:41:35,246
They conceded
to all your demands.

806
00:41:35,248 --> 00:41:38,116
Every single one.
How did you do it?

807
00:41:38,118 --> 00:41:39,867
Well, remember
that thumb drive

808
00:41:39,869 --> 00:41:41,485
we found in Bertram's
wine cellar?

809
00:41:41,487 --> 00:41:42,754
The encrypted database?

810
00:41:42,756 --> 00:41:45,189
It's a list
of Blake Association members.

811
00:41:45,191 --> 00:41:46,490
I used it as leverage.

812
00:41:46,492 --> 00:41:47,925
But we never broke
the encryption.

813
00:41:47,927 --> 00:41:50,128
Yeah,
the F.B.I. doesn't know that.

814
00:41:51,997 --> 00:41:53,965
That's why you escaped.

815
00:41:53,967 --> 00:41:55,600
To create a bogus list
of names.

816
00:41:55,602 --> 00:41:59,187
And to enjoy a bacon-wrapped
hot dog.

817
00:41:59,189 --> 00:42:01,773
I have to say,
I am impressed.

818
00:42:01,775 --> 00:42:04,692
- You outplayed the F.B.I.
-  No contest.

819
00:42:04,694 --> 00:42:06,227
Did they tell you
when I start work?

820
00:42:06,229 --> 00:42:08,946
When <i>we</i> start.

821
00:42:08,948 --> 00:42:10,314
<i>We?</i>

822
00:42:10,316 --> 00:42:11,616
What about your job?

823
00:42:11,618 --> 00:42:13,701
Nah. It was boring.
Yeah, I told you.

824
00:42:13,703 --> 00:42:15,536
Yeah. But you had
no right to.

825
00:42:15,538 --> 00:42:17,321
It's my life, and I'll decide
what to do with it.

826
00:42:17,323 --> 00:42:20,024
And you decided correctly.
There was never any choice.

827
00:42:20,026 --> 00:42:21,876
Oh, come on. It'll be fun.

828
00:42:21,878 --> 00:42:23,828
Let's see what kind
of trouble we can make.

829
00:42:23,830 --> 00:42:25,529
I got you something.

830
00:42:25,531 --> 00:42:26,864
For me?

831
00:42:26,866 --> 00:42:28,833
Mm-hmm.

832
00:42:36,141 --> 00:42:38,009
You got me socks.

833
00:42:38,011 --> 00:42:40,678
Handmade in Washington.

834
00:42:41,730 --> 00:42:43,564
Oh...

835
00:42:43,589 --> 00:42:48,589
